Description: Implements a robust multivariate statistical process control
    methodology for batch manufacturing that combines Minimum Covariance
    Determinant (MCD) estimation per batch with Multiple Factor Analysis
    (AFM) weighting. The methodology detects masking effects produced by
    outlier contamination in Phase I calibration data and preserves
    sensitivity to mean shifts in Phase II monitoring. The package
    provides bootstrap-calibrated upper control limits, baseline
    comparison with classical Hotelling T-squared and Vargas (2003)
    robust T-squared, and visual diagnostic panels based on
    Mason-Tracy-Young (1995) decomposition and confidence ellipses.
    Methodology based on Ruiz-Barzola et al. (2026) and
    Rousseeuw and Van Driessen (1999) <doi:10.1080/00401706.1999.10485670>.
